1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
This mandate has expired, and nobody is sitting around to close it.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Closing temporary onchain programs still means chasing signers,
checking old permissions, and proving nothing was left behind.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The owner fixes the treasury and close date, registers the obligations
and permissions, then signs one bounded authorization.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:43,000
After expiry, the worker re-reads Sepolia, chooses one permitted action,
simulates it, and submits it through KeeperHub.

5
00:00:43,000 --> 00:01:02,000
After every receipt, the agent reads the chain again before moving forward,
so a restart cannot become a duplicate payment.

6
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Every row links to a real Sepolia transaction: zero vault balance,
zero allowance, and the executor replaced by the zero address.

7
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Every approved obligation resolved, every residual asset returned,
and no agent authority left behind.
